"synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Ireland, UK","register":"Ireland, UK","wordFamily":["Hoover bag","Hoover blanket","Hooverette","Hoover flag","Hoover hog","Hooverize","Hooverizer","Hoover shoe","Hooverville","Hoover wagon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hoover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9e233a553506f2df8f","definition":"To clean (a room, etc.) with a vacuum cleaner, irrespective of the brand.","example":"I need to hoover this room.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vacuum"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Ireland, UK, ambitransitive","register":"Ireland, UK, ambitransitive","wordFamily":["Hoover bag","Hoover blanket","Hooverette","Hoover flag","Hoover hog","Hooverize","Hooverizer","Hoover shoe","Hooverville","Hoover wagon","hoover up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hoover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb2b4b7d99403d078b","definition":"To use a vacuum cleaner, irrespective of brand.","example":"I'd hoover, iron or dust, but I hated doing windows.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Ireland, UK","register":"Ireland, UK, intransitive","wordFamily":["Hoover bag","Hoover blanket","Hooverette","Hoover flag","Hoover hog","Hooverize","Hooverizer","Hoover shoe","Hooverville","Hoover wagon","hoover up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hoover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bf7d2e75e715fcd8b4","definition":"To suck in or inhale, as if by a vacuum cleaner.","example":"'You're probably thinking I'm a slob,' said Lister, finishing off a quintuple-thick milkshake and hoovering around the base with the straw.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"coll